Hmmm!  Nice case!  Of course, some first transistor must have been invented=
 that all the others copied and improved upon, but that doesn't really dodg=
e your point.  At the moment, I don't know what to suggest, except to hope =
that Lojban still has a word for kinds.  Bunches are, inter alia, Lesniewsk=
i's wholes (but xorxes doesn't like this kind of objectifying, preferring p=
lural reference, which works the same way formally).  I don't take 1a to be=
 about kinds, but just about     some unspecified bunch of lions (at least =
in Lojban, lo cinfo).  Kinds don't seem to be the sort of things that ruin =
gardens, though their exemplars may.  The factual situation, as far as tran=
sistors, etc. are concerned, is about genealogy, all transistors descend fr=
om something invented by Shockley.  But that is at least as hard to express=
 as types, so I wait a while on it.

